    "title": "<p><strong>Box&nbsp;10.02</strong> The Chompret criteria for <em>TP53</em> germline testing, amended in line with 2019 WHO Classification of Tumours terminology {26014290}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Breast tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2019. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 2). https://publications.iarc.who.int/581.",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 59.9%; background: #DAEEF3; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"59%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Familial presentation:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> Proband with a tumour belonging to the Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome tumour spectrum (cancers of the breast, soft tissue, bone, brain, or adrenal glands) at age &lt;&nbsp;46&nbsp;years; <strong>AND</strong> at least one first- or second-degree relative with a Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome tumour (with the exception of breast cancer if the proband has breast cancer) at age &lt;&nbsp;56&nbsp;years, or with multiple tumours</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Multiple primary tumours:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> Proband with multiple tumours (with the exception of multiple breast tumours), two of which belong to the Li&ndash;Fraumeni syndrome tumour spectrum&nbsp;&ndash; the first of which occurred at age &lt;&nbsp;46&nbsp;years</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Rare tumours:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> Patient with embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma, choroid plexus tumour, or adrenocortical carcinoma, irrespective of family history</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 100.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"100%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Early-onset breast cancer:</span></strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"> Breast cancer occurring at age &lt;&nbsp;31&nbsp;years</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
